# Lab 1 — Trojan / Remote Access Trojan

This lab explored how **Remote Access Trojans (RATs)** can be used to gain unauthorized remote access to a target system. In a controlled virtual lab environment, I studied how a Trojan can establish a covert communication channel and provide remote access to system information and user activity.

The exercise focused on understanding the capabilities and risks associated with RATs, including remote system access, process monitoring, screen capture, keylogging, and other forms of system surveillance. The lab also demonstrated how these techniques can be used by security professionals as a controlled proof of concept to evaluate defensive security controls.

**Key Concepts:** `Trojans` • `RATs` • `Remote Access` • `Keylogging` • `System Monitoring` • `Malware` • `Security Controls`


